===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|psychrometre}} {{qualifier|nonstandard, rare}}

===Etymology===
{{confix|en|psychro|meter}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|meteorology}} Any of several instruments used to measure the [[relative humidity]] of the [[atmosphere]]; especially a [[wet-and-dry-bulb hygrometer]].
#* '''1982''' July, Ray W. Brown, Dale L. Bartos, ''A Calibration Model for Screen-caged Peltier Thermocouple '''Psychrometers''''', {{w|United States Department of Agriculture}}: {{w|United States Forest Service|Forest Service}}, Research Paper INT-293, [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=BGnpPYgkC6AC&pg=PA2&dq=%22psychrometer%22%7C%22psychrometers%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjOoY3Sx5n9AhW0k2oFHR4-BUcQ6AF6BAhkEAI#v=onepage&q=%22psychrometer%22%7C%22psychrometers%22&f=false page 2],
#*: Gross adjustment of the model using a small number of well controlled calibration measurements would suffice to make the model applicable to any new '''psychrometer''' or group of '''psychrometers'''.
#* '''2007''', N. J. Livingston, G. Clarke Topp, ''71: Soil Water Potential'', M. R. Carter, E. G. Gregorich (editors), ''Soil Sampling and Methods of Analysis'', 2nd Edition, {{w|Canadian Society of Soil Science}}, Taylor & Francis (CRC Press), [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=ZTJsbXsikagC&pg=PA976&dq=%22psychrometer%22%7C%22psychrometers%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjOoY3Sx5n9AhW0k2oFHR4-BUcQ6AF6BAg0EAI#v=onepage&q=%22psychrometer%22%7C%22psychrometers%22&f=false page 976],
#*: '''Psychrometers''' have two main components: the porous cup with its contained sensing and reference junctions and the instrument for generating the electrical current and measuring the '''psychrometer''' output.
#* '''2008''', Ross Montgomery, Robert McDowall, ''Fundamentals of [[HVAC]] Control Systems'', {{w|ASHRAE|American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air-Conditioning Engineers}}, Elsevier, [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=UMk1EUp-W-UC&pg=PA132&dq=%22psychrometer%22%7C%22psychrometers%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjOoY3Sx5n9AhW0k2oFHR4-BUcQ6AF6BAhdEAI#v=onepage&q=%22psychrometer%22%7C%22psychrometers%22&f=false page 132],
#*: An aspirated '''psychrometer''' combines low cost with the fundamental measurement principle of wet- and dry-bulb readings.

